{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The locking nut assortment fits my interest in keeping useful repair supplies on hand, much like my hose clamp and electrical connector assortments.",
    "The caliper would help me measure fittings and hardware before choosing replacement parts, giving it a clear purpose alongside my repair supplies."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Printer filament requires a printing project that my history does not establish; buying tape, clamps, and cement does not create that need.",
    "Different filament colors, shiny finishes, and a large bundle do not solve a current repair problem for me, so none gives me a reason to choose it."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in practical tools and repair materials seems to have been stretched into an assumed interest in 3D printing.",
    "The repeated filament choices seem to treat materials for making things as interchangeable with supplies for fixing existing things."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated clamp purchases and connector assortment point toward securing, joining, and replacing parts, which makes useful fasteners a closer match.",
    "I need a clear practical use before choosing a supply; filament compatibility or color matters only after I actually need to print something."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in repair hardware, but assumed a need for 3D printing supplies that my purchases do not support."
}"}
